Over the 14,927 returning requests the arm sent before minute 110 (All four rules): mean TTFT 10.96 s. Requests served in 2 h:
17,093; users admitted: 678 of the 729 that arrive.
Recorded waits at x1, one run per arm. 0.1 users arrive a second and at most 128 are in session; the others wait for a slot, a wait
TTFT leaves out. Prompts are synthetic token ids of the recorded lengths and outputs have the recorded length; sessions with a
request over 65,536 tokens are left out. Exact hints are the true next-request times; p50 hints are the median wait after the tool
call the reply makes, from a table the client keeps online for each harness and model. The rules arm gets that table's p10, p50 and
p90 and an end-of-session signal: it starts reads by expected cost at a learned price on host memory, evicts by chance of return,
and lets an arrived request's read take room from early reads. Attention runs on FlashAttention 3. Engine fixes on: pages the SSD
already holds are not written again; queued writes are merged into transfers of up to 128 pages; timed reads wait while pending
writes hold 50,000 host tokens; a read refused host memory is retried without spending the turn's lookups.
